---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Values Planner" active="values-planner" pageMark="🧭" eyebrow="Tools"
  description="Pick laws, government reforms and estate privileges and see where your societal values drift, and how long it takes.">

  <p style="max-width: 780px; color: var(--text-soft);">
    Societal values sit on a −100…+100 axis, and every law, estate privilege,
    cabinet action or building applies a monthly push toward one pole. Pick
    what you run and this sums the push per axis and shows what it can unlock.
    Magnitudes are the game's own — tiny 0.025, minor 0.05, normal 0.1, large
    0.2, significant 0.33 per month.
  </p>
  <p style="max-width: 780px; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13px;">
    <b>A value stalls at 100 × its net monthly push</b>
    (<code>SOCIETAL_VALUE_INERTIA_SCALE</code>, confirmed by player testing):
    0.3/month of push carries you to ±30 and no further, and drift slows on
    the way there. Remove the push and the value drifts back toward whatever
    the remaining setup supports — nothing about the position itself is
    banked. The projections here use that curve.
  </p>
  <p style="max-width: 780px; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13px;">
    Mind what a reform demands: one whose requirement is a
    <code>societal_values</code> focus block needs the value <b>held at 50
    toward its pole — the game removes the reform when that stops being
    true</b>. Only a reform whose requirement sits in its <code>allow</code>
    block appears to survive the value drifting back (verify in game). Laws
    and privileges push only while you run them. For sequencing several
    targets against the campaign clock, use the Value Path tool.
  </p>

  <div class="vp" data-vp>
    <div class="vp-controls">
      <div class="pl-picker" data-vp-country>
        <input type="search" placeholder="Pick a country…" autocomplete="off" />
        <div class="hdr-search__results" hidden></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pl-picker" data-vp-culture hidden>
        <input type="search" autocomplete="off" />
        <div class="hdr-search__results" hidden></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pl-picker" data-vp-religion hidden>
        <input type="search" autocomplete="off" />
        <div class="hdr-search__results" hidden></div>
      </div>
      <span class="chips" data-vp-context></span>
      <button type="button" class="csv-btn" data-vp-reset title="Back to this country's 1337 setup">↺ 1337 setup</button>
      <label class="pl-toggle" title="Include things your country cannot take">
        <input type="checkbox" data-vp-all /> show unavailable
      </label>
      <label class="pl-toggle" title="Efficiency of a cabinet member on Encourage Societal Value — base push is 1.0/month × this">
        cabinet eff. <input type="number" data-vp-eff value="0.4" min="0" max="1" step="0.05"
          style="width:56px; background:var(--bg-elev); color:var(--text); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:3px; padding:2px 5px; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px;" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="vp-controls">
      <input type="search" data-vp-q placeholder="Search laws, reforms, privileges, buildings…" autocomplete="off" />
      <span class="chips" data-vp-sources></span>
      <span class="pl-spacer"></span>
      <button type="button" class="csv-btn" data-vp-copy>⧉ Copy link</button>
      <button type="button" class="csv-btn" data-vp-clear>✕ Clear</button>
    </div>

    <div class="vp-grid">
      <section class="vp-pane">
        <h2 class="vp-h">Your picks <small data-vp-count>none</small></h2>
        <div class="vp-picked" data-vp-picked></div>
        <h2 class="vp-h" style="margin-top:18px;">Available</h2>
        <div class="vp-list" data-vp-list></div>
      </section>

      <section class="vp-pane">
        <h2 class="vp-h">Drift
          <small>from your starting position, at <span data-vp-yrs>20</span> years —
          <input type="range" min="1" max="100" value="20" data-vp-years /></small>
        </h2>
        <div class="vp-axes" data-vp-axes></div>
        <h2 class="vp-h" style="margin-top:18px;">Unlocks along the way
          <small data-vp-unlocked></small></h2>
        <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-faint); margin:-4px 0 8px;">
          Timed with the stall curve: drift slows toward its equilibrium of
          100 × net push, so anything past that stalls out. A focus-block
          reform needs its 50 <em>held</em> — the game removes it when the
          value drops back; only <code>allow</code>-gated requirements appear
          to be start-only (verify in game).
        </p>
        <div class="vp-unlocks" data-vp-unlocks></div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style is:global>
    .vp-controls { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 16px; }
    .vp-controls input {
      background: var(--bg-elev); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 11px; font-size: 13px;
      width: 300px; font-family: var(--font-ui);
    }
    .vp-controls input:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--gold-deep); }
    .vp-controls .chip { cursor: pointer; }
    .vp-controls .chip.on { background: var(--gold-glow); border-color: var(--gold-deep); color: var(--gold); }

    .vp-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap: 22px; margin-top: 14px; }
    @media (max-width: 980px) { .vp-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    .vp-h { font-size: 15px; color: var(--gold-soft); margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .vp-h small { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-faint); margin-left: 8px; }
    .vp-pane { min-width: 0; }
    .vp-list, .vp-picked { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; max-height: 62vh; overflow-y: auto; }
    .vp-list { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px; background: var(--bg-elev); }

    .vp-item {
      display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; padding: 4px 8px;
      border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; border-left: 2px solid transparent;
      font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-soft);
    }
    .vp-item:hover { background: var(--bg-elev-2); border-left-color: var(--gold); }
    .vp-item.on { background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--gold) 14%, var(--bg-elev-2)); border-left-color: var(--gold); }
    .vp-item .src { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: 11px; }
    .vp-item .eff { margin-left: auto; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; white-space: nowrap; }
    .vp-item .eff b { font-weight: 600; }
    .vp-item.dim { opacity: .42; }
    .vp-item .eicon { flex: none; }
    .chip.shifted { cursor: pointer; border-color: var(--gold-deep); color: var(--gold-soft); }

    .vp-axis { margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .vp-axis__top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 3px; }
    .vp-axis__l { color: var(--text-soft); }
    .vp-axis__r { color: var(--text-soft); }
    .vp-axis__bar {
      position: relative; height: 12px; background: var(--bg-elev-2);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden;
    }
    .vp-axis__mid { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 1px; background: var(--border-strong); }
    .vp-axis__fill { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; background: var(--gold); opacity: .85; }
    .vp-axis__num { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-faint); margin-top: 2px; }
    .vp-axis__num b { color: var(--gold); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
    .vp-axis.quiet { opacity: .45; }
    .vp-axis__start {
      width: 46px; background: var(--bg-elev); color: var(--text);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 4px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px;
    }
    .vp-axis__now { position: absolute; top: -2px; bottom: -2px; width: 2px; background: var(--text); opacity: .8; }
    .vp-h input[type=range] { vertical-align: middle; width: 110px; }
    .vp-unlocks { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; max-height: 40vh; overflow-y: auto; }
    .vp-unlock { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: baseline; font-size: 12.5px; padding: 3px 8px;
      border-left: 2px solid var(--good); border-radius: 3px; background: var(--bg-elev-2); }
    .vp-unlock.later { border-left-color: var(--gold-deep); }
    .vp-unlock.never { border-left-color: var(--border-strong); opacity: .5; }
    .vp-unlock .when { margin-left: auto; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-faint); }
  </style>

  <script>
    const root = document.querySelector('[data-vp]')!;
    const $ = (s: string) => root.querySelector(s) as HTMLElement;
    const baseUrl = document.querySelector('.site-title a')!.getAttribute('href')!;

    let D: any = null;
    let STARTS: any = {};                       // tag -> 1337 setup
    const picked = new Set<string>();
    let sourceFilter: string | null = null;
    let horizonYears = 20;
    let country: any = null;
    let culOverride: any = null;
    let relOverride: any = null;
    let showUnavailable = false;
    let cabEff = 0.4;                           // Encourage push = 1.0 × this
    const start: Record<string, number> = {};   // where each axis begins
    const esc = (t: string) => String(t).replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) =>
      ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' } as any)[c]);
    const uid = (m: any) => `${m.folder}:${m.key}`;

    /** Adopt a country's 1337 setup: where each axis begins, and the laws
     *  and privileges it already runs. Straight from the bookmark's template
     *  stack, so it is the position you actually start the game in. */
    function adoptStart(tag: string | null) {
      picked.clear();
      for (const k of Object.keys(start)) delete start[k];
      const rec = tag && STARTS[tag];
      if (!rec) return;
      Object.assign(start, rec.values || {});
      const want = new Set([...(rec.privileges || []),
                            ...Object.values(rec.laws || {})]);
      for (const m of D.movers) if (want.has(m.key)) picked.add(uid(m));
    }

    /** Country facts with any culture/religion swap applied. */
    function facts() {
      if (!country) return null;
      const rec = STARTS[country.t] || {};
      const f = { ...country.f, cap: country.f.cap || {},
                  gov: rec.type || null,
                  io: rec.io || [], parl: rec.parliament || null,
                  laws: new Set(Object.values(rec.laws || {})),
                  privs: new Set(rec.privileges || []) };
      if (culOverride) { f.cul = culOverride.k; f.cgrp = culOverride.g; f.lang = culOverride.l; }
      if (relOverride) { f.rel = relOverride.k; f.rgrp = relOverride.g; }
      return f;
    }
    /** TRUE / FALSE / null-unknown, matching the value-path evaluator. */
    function evalGate(e: any, f: any): boolean | null {
      if (!e) return true;
      const h = e[0];
      if (h === 'and') { let u = false; for (const s of e.slice(1)) { const v = evalGate(s, f); if (v === false) return false; if (v === null) u = true; } return u ? null : true; }
      if (h === 'or') { let u = false; for (const s of e.slice(1)) { const v = evalGate(s, f); if (v === true) return true; if (v === null) u = true; } return u ? null : false; }
      if (h === 'not') { const v = evalGate(e[1], f); return v === null ? null : !v; }
      if (h === '?' || h === 'var' || h === 'policy' || h === 'unl' ||
          h === 'adv' || h === 'age' || h === 'age>=' || h === 'reform') return null;
      if (h === 'true') return true;
      if (h === 'false') return false;
      if (h === 'cap') return (f.cap || {})[e[1]] === e[2];
      if (h === 'cgrp') return (f.cgrp || []).includes(e[1]);
      if (h === 'tag') return f.tag === e[1];
      if (h === 'gov') return f.gov ? f.gov === e[1] : null;
      if (h === 'iotype') return false;
      if (h === 'iomem') return (f.io || []).includes(e[1]) ? true : null;
      if (h === 'mrep') return f.gov === 'republic' ? null : false;
      if (h === 'ctype') return false;
      if (h === 'law') return f.laws && f.laws.has(e[1]) ? true : null;
      if (h === 'priv') return f.privs && f.privs.has(e[1]) ? true : null;
      if (h === 'parl') return f.parl ? f.parl === e[1] : null;
      return f[h] === e[1];
    }
    /** Can this country take it? Unknown counts as yes — it depends on
     *  state you can still acquire. */
    function usable(m: any) {
      const f = facts();
      if (!f || !m.gate) return true;
      return evalGate(m.gate, f) !== false;
    }

    /** One effect's monthly weight: Encourage scales with cabinet
     *  efficiency, estate-power-tiered effects count at half. */
    const effVal = (m: any, e: any) =>
      (e.perMonth ?? 0) * (m.encourage ? cabEff : 1) * (e.scaled ? 0.5 : 1);

    /** Net monthly drift per axis. Right is positive, left negative — the
     *  same convention as the -100..+100 axis itself. */
    function totals() {
      const out: Record<string, number> = {};
      for (const m of D.movers) {
        if (!picked.has(uid(m))) continue;
        for (const e of m.effects) {
          if (e.temp) continue;              // only while a debate runs
          const v = effVal(m, e) * (e.dir === 'right' ? 1 : -1);
          out[e.pair] = (out[e.pair] || 0) + v;
        }
      }
      return out;
    }
    /** Push toward each pole and how many factors supply it — the game says
     *  the ceiling is set by the total amount of factors, so both matter. */
    function sides() {
      const out: Record<string, { l: number; r: number; n: number }> = {};
      for (const m of D.movers) {
        if (!picked.has(uid(m))) continue;
        for (const e of m.effects) {
          if (e.temp) continue;
          const s = out[e.pair] || (out[e.pair] = { l: 0, r: 0, n: 0 });
          if (e.dir === 'right') s.r += effVal(m, e); else s.l += effVal(m, e);
          s.n++;
        }
      }
      return out;
    }

    function effLabel(m: any) {
      return m.effects.map((e: any) => {
        const p = D.pairs[e.pair];
        const side = e.dir === 'right' ? p.right.name : p.left.name;
        return `<b>${+effVal(m, e).toFixed(3)}</b>→${esc(side)}`;
      }).join(' ');
    }

    function itemHtml(m: any) {
      const dim = !usable(m) ? ' dim' : '';
      const icon = m.icon
        ? `<img class="eicon" src="${baseUrl}${m.icon}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="16" height="16"/>` : '';
      const est = m.estate ? `<span class="src">${esc(m.estate)}</span>` : '';
      return `<div class="vp-item ${picked.has(uid(m)) ? 'on' : ''}${dim}" data-uid="${esc(uid(m))}">` +
        icon + `<span>${esc(m.name)}</span>` +
        `<span class="src">${esc(m.groupName || m.source)}</span>${est}` +
        `<span class="eff">${effLabel(m)}</span></div>`;
    }

    function renderList() {
      const term = ($('[data-vp-q]') as HTMLInputElement).value.trim().toLowerCase();
      const hits = D.movers.filter((m: any) =>
        (showUnavailable || usable(m)) &&
        (!sourceFilter || m.source === sourceFilter) &&
        (!term || m.name.toLowerCase().includes(term) ||
         m.source.toLowerCase().includes(term) ||
         m.effects.some((e: any) => {
           const p = D.pairs[e.pair];
           return p.left.name.toLowerCase().includes(term) ||
                  p.right.name.toLowerCase().includes(term);
         })));
      $('[data-vp-list]').innerHTML = hits.slice(0, 400).map(itemHtml).join('') ||
        '<div class="pl-empty">Nothing matches.</div>';
    }

    function renderPicked() {
      const list = D.movers.filter((m: any) => picked.has(uid(m)));
      $('[data-vp-count]').textContent = list.length ? `${list.length} selected` : 'none';
      $('[data-vp-picked]').innerHTML = list.map(itemHtml).join('') ||
        '<div style="color:var(--text-faint); font-size:12.5px; padding:4px 8px;">' +
        'Nothing picked yet — choose from the list below.</div>';
    }

    /** The drift model (same as the value path): a value approaches an
     *  equilibrium of INERTIA × net push, at (E − v)/INERTIA per month, with
     *  the engine's 0.01 floor carrying the last point. */
    const INERTIA = () => D.inertia || 100;
    const MIN_MOVE = 0.01;
    const eqOf = (net: number) => net * INERTIA();
    /** Where an axis sits after n months, clamped to the -100..100 range. */
    function positionAt(pid: string, net: number, months: number) {
      const v0 = start[pid] ?? 0;
      const E = eqOf(net);
      const v = E + (v0 - E) * Math.exp(-months / INERTIA());
      return Math.max(-D.scale, Math.min(D.scale, v));
    }
    /** Months until a requirement is met, or null if this drift stalls
     *  short of it (already-met returns 0). */
    function monthsUntil(req: any, net: number) {
      const v0 = start[req.pair] ?? 0;
      const T = req.value;
      const ok = (v: number) => req.op === '>' ? v > T : req.op === '>=' ? v >= T
        : req.op === '<' ? v < T : req.op === '<=' ? v <= T : v === T;
      if (ok(v0)) return 0;
      if (!net) return null;
      const E = eqOf(net);
      const toward = T > v0 ? 1 : -1;
      if ((E - v0) * toward <= 0 || (E - T) * toward < 0) return null;
      if ((E - T) * toward >= 1) return INERTIA() * Math.log((E - v0) / (E - T));
      const edge = E - toward;
      const expo = (edge - v0) * toward > 0
        ? INERTIA() * Math.log(Math.abs(E - v0)) : 0;
      const crawlFrom = (edge - v0) * toward > 0 ? edge : v0;
      return expo + Math.abs(T - crawlFrom) / MIN_MOVE;
    }

    function renderAxes() {
      const t = totals();
      const sideTotals = sides();
      const months = horizonYears * 12;
      const rows = Object.entries(D.pairs).map(([pid, p]: any) => {
        const net = t[pid] || 0;
        const now = positionAt(pid, net, months);
        const sd = sideTotals[pid] || { l: 0, r: 0, n: 0 };
        const pct = Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, net / 0.6));
        const w = Math.abs(pct) * 50;
        const left = net >= 0 ? 50 : 50 - w;
        return { pid, p, net, now, sd, w, left };
      });
      rows.sort((a, b) => Math.abs(b.net) - Math.abs(a.net) ||
        a.p.left.name.localeCompare(b.p.left.name));
      $('[data-vp-axes]').innerHTML = rows.map((r) =>
        `<div class="vp-axis ${r.net ? '' : 'quiet'}">` +
        `<div class="vp-axis__top"><span class="vp-axis__l">${esc(r.p.left.name)}</span>` +
        `<span class="vp-axis__r">${esc(r.p.right.name)}</span></div>` +
        `<div class="vp-axis__bar"><div class="vp-axis__mid"></div>` +
        (r.net ? `<div class="vp-axis__fill" style="left:${r.left}%; width:${r.w}%"></div>` : '') +
        `<div class="vp-axis__now" style="left:${50 + (r.now / D.scale) * 50}%"></div>` +
        `</div>` +
        `<div class="vp-axis__num">` +
        `<span>start <input class="vp-axis__start" type="number" step="5" min="-100" max="100" ` +
        `value="${start[r.pid] ?? 0}" data-start="${r.pid}" /> → <b>${r.now.toFixed(1)}</b> at ${horizonYears} yrs</span>` +
        (r.net ? `<span title="push: ${r.sd.l.toFixed(3)} left / ${r.sd.r.toFixed(3)} right from ${r.sd.n} factor(s)">` +
                 `${r.net > 0 ? '+' : ''}${r.net.toFixed(3)}/month from ${r.sd.n} · ` +
                 `stalls at ${Math.max(-D.scale, Math.min(D.scale, Math.round(eqOf(r.net))))}</span>`
               : '<span>no push — drifts toward 0</span>') +
        `</div></div>`).join('');
    }

    /** What your picks eventually qualify you for, and roughly when. */
    function renderUnlocks() {
      const t = totals();
      const horizon = horizonYears * 12;
      const rows: any[] = [];
      for (const r of D.requirements) {
        let worst: number | null = 0;
        let impossible = false;
        for (const req of r.requires) {
          if (!(req.pair in D.pairs)) continue;
          const m = monthsUntil(req, t[req.pair] || 0);
          if (m === null) { impossible = true; break; }
          worst = Math.max(worst as number, m);
        }
        if (impossible || worst === null) { rows.push({ r, months: null }); continue; }
        rows.push({ r, months: worst });
      }
      const reachable = rows.filter((x) => x.months !== null && x.months <= horizon);
      reachable.sort((a, b) => a.months - b.months);
      const rest = rows.filter((x) => !(x.months !== null && x.months <= horizon));
      $('[data-vp-unlocked]').textContent =
        `${reachable.length} within ${horizonYears} years · ${rows.length} gated in total`;
      $('[data-vp-unlocks]').innerHTML = [...reachable, ...rest.slice(0, 40)].map((x: any) => {
        const cls = x.months === null ? 'never' : x.months === 0 ? '' : 'later';
        const hold = x.r.requires.some((q: any) => q.hold);
        const when = (x.months === null ? 'this drift stalls short of it'
          : x.months === 0 ? 'already qualifies'
          : `no sooner than ${(x.months / 12).toFixed(1)} yrs`) +
          (hold && x.months !== null ? ' · must stay held or the reform is lost' : '');
        const need = x.r.requires.map((q: any) => {
          const p = D.pairs[q.pair];
          return p ? `${esc(p.left.name)}/${esc(p.right.name)} ${q.op} ${q.value}` : q.pair;
        }).join(', ');
        const link = x.r.id ? `${baseUrl}${x.r.folder === 'laws' ? 'laws' :
          x.r.folder === 'government_reforms' ? 'reforms' :
          x.r.folder === 'estate_privileges' ? 'privileges' : ''}/${x.r.slug}` : null;
        const label = link ? `<a href="${link}">${esc(x.r.name)}</a>` : esc(x.r.name);
        return `<div class="vp-unlock ${cls}">${label}` +
          `<span class="src" style="color:var(--text-faint);font-size:11px">${esc(x.r.source)}</span>` +
          `<span class="when" title="${esc(need)}">${when}</span></div>`;
      }).join('');
    }

    function syncUrl() {
      const p = new URLSearchParams();
      if (country) p.set('c', country.t);
      if (culOverride) p.set('cu', culOverride.k);
      if (relOverride) p.set('re', relOverride.k);
      if (picked.size) p.set('p', [...picked].join(','));
      const st = Object.entries(start).filter(([, v]) => v);
      if (st.length) p.set('s', st.map(([k, v]) => `${k}:${v}`).join(','));
      if (horizonYears !== 20) p.set('y', String(horizonYears));
      history.replaceState(null, '', p.toString() ? '?' + p.toString() : location.pathname);
    }
    function renderContext() {
      const cw = $('[data-vp-culture]'), rw = $('[data-vp-religion]');
      cw.hidden = rw.hidden = !country;
      if (!country) { $('[data-vp-context]').innerHTML = ''; return; }
      let html = `<span class="chip" style="border-color:${country.col ?? 'var(--border)'}">${esc(country.n)}</span>`;
      if (culOverride) html += `<span class="chip shifted" data-reset="cul">${esc(culOverride.n)} ✕</span>`;
      if (relOverride) html += `<span class="chip shifted" data-reset="rel">${esc(relOverride.n)} ✕</span>`;
      (cw.querySelector('input') as HTMLInputElement).placeholder =
        `Culture: ${culOverride ? culOverride.n : country.cu}`;
      (rw.querySelector('input') as HTMLInputElement).placeholder =
        `Religion: ${relOverride ? relOverride.n : country.re}`;
      $('[data-vp-context]').innerHTML = html;
    }

    function wirePicker(sel: string, items: (q: string) => any[], onPick: (k: string) => void) {
      const wrap = $(sel);
      const input = wrap.querySelector('input') as HTMLInputElement;
      const results = wrap.querySelector('.hdr-search__results') as HTMLElement;
      const refresh = () => {
        const q = input.value.trim().toLowerCase();
        if (!q) { results.hidden = true; return; }
        const hits = items(q).slice(0, 12);
        results.innerHTML = hits.map((h: any) =>
          `<a href="#" data-key="${esc(h.key)}"><span>${esc(h.label)}</span><small>${esc(h.small || '')}</small></a>`).join('');
        results.hidden = hits.length === 0;
      };
      input.addEventListener('input', refresh);
      input.addEventListener('focus', refresh);
      results.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const a = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('[data-key]') as HTMLElement | null;
        if (!a) return;
        onPick(a.dataset.key!);
        input.value = ''; results.hidden = true;
        render();
      });
      document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        if (!wrap.contains(e.target as Node)) results.hidden = true;
      });
    }

    function render() { renderContext(); renderList(); renderPicked(); renderAxes(); renderUnlocks(); syncUrl(); }

    Promise.all([
      fetch(`${baseUrl}values.json`).then((r) => r.json()),
      fetch(`${baseUrl}country-start.json`).then((r) => r.json()).catch(() => ({})),
    ]).then(([data, starts]) => {
      D = data;
      STARTS = starts;
      const sources = [...new Set(D.movers.map((m: any) => m.source))].sort();
      $('[data-vp-sources]').innerHTML = sources.map((s: any) =>
        `<span class="chip" data-src="${esc(s)}">${esc(s)}</span>`).join('');
      $('[data-vp-sources]').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const c = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('[data-src]') as HTMLElement | null;
        if (!c) return;
        sourceFilter = sourceFilter === c.dataset.src ? null : c.dataset.src!;
        for (const x of root.querySelectorAll('[data-src]')) x.classList.remove('on');
        if (sourceFilter) c.classList.add('on');
        renderList();
      });

      wirePicker('[data-vp-country]',
        (q) => D.countries.filter((c: any) => c.n.toLowerCase().includes(q) || c.t.toLowerCase() === q)
          .map((c: any) => ({ key: c.t, label: c.n, small: `${c.cu} · ${c.re}` })),
        (tag) => {
          country = D.countries.find((c: any) => c.t === tag) || null;
          culOverride = relOverride = null;
          adoptStart(tag);
        });
      wirePicker('[data-vp-culture]',
        (q) => D.cultures.filter((c: any) => c.n.toLowerCase().includes(q))
          .map((c: any) => ({ key: c.k, label: c.n, small: 'culture' })),
        (k) => { culOverride = D.cultures.find((c: any) => c.k === k) || null; });
      wirePicker('[data-vp-religion]',
        (q) => D.religions.filter((r: any) => r.n.toLowerCase().includes(q))
          .map((r: any) => ({ key: r.k, label: r.n, small: 'religion' })),
        (k) => { relOverride = D.religions.find((r: any) => r.k === k) || null; });
      $('[data-vp-context]').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const c = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('[data-reset]') as HTMLElement | null;
        if (!c) return;
        if (c.dataset.reset === 'cul') culOverride = null; else relOverride = null;
        render();
      });
      ($('[data-vp-all]') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
        showUnavailable = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked; renderList();
      });
      ($('[data-vp-eff]') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
        const v = parseFloat((e.target as HTMLInputElement).value);
        if (Number.isFinite(v)) { cabEff = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, v)); render(); }
      });

      const qs = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      const q = qs.get('p');
      if (q) for (const id of q.split(',')) picked.add(id);
      country = D.countries.find((c: any) => c.t === qs.get('c')) || null;
      if (country && !q) adoptStart(country.t);
      culOverride = D.cultures.find((c: any) => c.k === qs.get('cu')) || null;
      relOverride = D.religions.find((r: any) => r.k === qs.get('re')) || null;
      for (const bit of (qs.get('s') || '').split(',').filter(Boolean)) {
        const [k, v] = bit.split(':');
        if (k in D.pairs) start[k] = parseFloat(v) || 0;
      }
      const y = parseInt(qs.get('y') || '', 10);
      if (!isNaN(y)) {
        horizonYears = Math.min(100, Math.max(1, y));
        ($('[data-vp-years]') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(horizonYears);
      }
      $('[data-vp-yrs]').textContent = String(horizonYears);
      render();
    });

    for (const sel of ['[data-vp-list]', '[data-vp-picked]']) {
      root.querySelector(sel)!.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const el = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('[data-uid]') as HTMLElement | null;
        if (!el) return;
        const id = el.dataset.uid!;
        if (picked.has(id)) {
          picked.delete(id);
        } else {
          picked.add(id);
          // One policy per law group — picking one drops its siblings.
          const m = D.movers.find((x: any) => uid(x) === id);
          if (m && m.group) {
            for (const o of D.movers) {
              if (o.group === m.group && uid(o) !== id) picked.delete(uid(o));
            }
          }
        }
        render();
      });
    }
    ($('[data-vp-q]') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('input', renderList);
    ($('[data-vp-years]') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('input', (e) => {
      horizonYears = parseInt((e.target as HTMLInputElement).value, 10);
      $('[data-vp-yrs]').textContent = String(horizonYears);
      renderAxes(); renderUnlocks(); syncUrl();
    });
    $('[data-vp-axes]').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
      const el = e.target as HTMLInputElement;
      if (!el.dataset.start) return;
      start[el.dataset.start] = parseFloat(el.value) || 0;
      renderAxes(); renderUnlocks(); syncUrl();
    });
    $('[data-vp-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (country) { adoptStart(country.t); render(); }
    });
    $('[data-vp-clear]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      picked.clear();
      for (const k of Object.keys(start)) delete start[k];
      render();
    });
    $('[data-vp-copy]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      syncUrl();
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(location.href);
      const b = $('[data-vp-copy]'); b.textContent = '✓ Copied';
      setTimeout(() => (b.textContent = '⧉ Copy link'), 1200);
    });
  </script>
</Base>
